# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Add errors to a noise model {#add-errors-to-a-noise-model}"
msgstr "Magdagdag ng mga error sa isang noise model {#add-errors-to-a-noise-model}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "When adding a quantum error to a noise model, we must specify the type of *instruction* that it acts on and what qubits to apply it to. There are two cases of quantum errors:\n"
msgstr "Kapag nagdadagdag ng quantum error sa isang noise model, kailangan nating tukuyin ang uri ng *instruction* na kinakatawan nito at kung aling mga qubit ang apektado. May dalawang uri ng quantum error:\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: ' 1. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "All-qubit quantum error\n"
msgstr "All-qubit quantum error\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: ' 2. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Specific qubit quantum error\n"
msgstr "Specific qubit quantum error\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "1. All-qubit quantum error {#1-all-qubit-quantum-error}"
msgstr "1. All-qubit quantum error {#1-all-qubit-quantum-error}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This applies the same error to any occurrence of an instruction, regardless of which qubits it acts on.\n"
msgstr "Inilalapat nito ang parehong error sa bawat pagkakataon ng isang instruction, anuman ang mga qubit na kinakatawan nito.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "It is added as `noise_model.add_all_qubit_quantum_error(error, instructions)`:\n"
msgstr "Idinaragdag ito bilang `noise_model.add_all_qubit_quantum_error(error, instructions)`:\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "2. Specific qubit quantum error {#2-specific-qubit-quantum-error}"
msgstr "2. Specific qubit quantum error {#2-specific-qubit-quantum-error}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This applies the error to any occurrence of an instruction acting on a specified list of qubits. Note that the order of the qubit matters: for example, an error applied to qubits [0, 1] for a two-qubit gate is different to one applied to qubits [1, 0].\n"
msgstr "Inilalapat nito ang error sa bawat pagkakataon ng isang instruction na kumikilos sa isang tinukoy na listahan ng mga qubit. Pansinin na mahalaga ang pagkakasunod ng mga qubit: halimbawa, ang isang error na inilapat sa mga qubit [0, 1] para sa isang two-qubit gate ay iba sa isang inilapat sa mga qubit [1, 0].\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "It is added as `noise_model.add_quantum_error(error, instructions, qubits)`:\n"
msgstr "Idinaragdag ito bilang `noise_model.add_quantum_error(error, instructions, qubits)`:\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Note on non-local qubit quantum error {#note-on-non-local-qubit-quantum-error}"
msgstr "Tala tungkol sa non-local qubit quantum error {#note-on-non-local-qubit-quantum-error}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "`NoiseModel` does not support addition of non-local qubit quantum errors. They should be handled outside of `NoiseModel`. That suggests you should [write your own transpiler pass](/guides/custom-transpiler-pass) (`TransformationPass`) and run the pass just before running the simulator if you need to insert your quantum errors into your circuit under your own conditions.\n"
msgstr "Hindi sinusuportahan ng `NoiseModel` ang pagdaragdag ng non-local qubit quantum errors. Dapat itong pangasiwaan sa labas ng `NoiseModel`. Ibig sabihin nito, kung kailangan mong ipasok ang iyong mga quantum error sa iyong circuit sa ilalim ng iyong sariling mga kundisyon, dapat kang [sumulat ng sariling transpiler pass](/guides/custom-transpiler-pass) (`TransformationPass`) at patakbuhin ang pass bago patakbuhin ang simulator.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Execute a noisy simulation with a noise model {#execute-a-noisy-simulation-with-a-noise-model}"
msgstr "Magpatakbo ng noisy simulation gamit ang isang noise model {#execute-a-noisy-simulation-with-a-noise-model}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The command `AerSimulator(noise_model=noise_model)` returns a simulator configured to the given noise model. In addition to setting the simulator's noise model, it also overrides the simulator's basis gates, according to the gates of the noise model.\n"
msgstr "Ang command na `AerSimulator(noise_model=noise_model)` ay nagbabalik ng simulator na naka-configure sa ibinigay na noise model. Bukod sa pag-set ng noise model ng simulator, ino-override din nito ang mga basis gate ng simulator, ayon sa mga gate ng noise model.\n"

